This way we don't need a mutex at all — each goroutine writes to its own pre-assigned slot. We still need synchronization for the error collection... but wait, each slot is owned by exactly one goroutine, so writing to `out[it.index]` is safe without a mutex. However, I was collecting errs in a slice with the mutex. Let me simplify by using the same indexed approach for errors.

